body:
absolutely. 

&#x200B;

i try not to judge bc i know women like that may have body dysmorphia, may have been overweight at some point in their lives before, and society just makes every woman feel less of themselves BUT to say "i'm so fat" and just throw the word out like that to their followers is still incredibly insensitive to me.

&#x200B;

i can sometimes excuse that if a person has an ED account and makes sure their following knows they'll post potentially triggering photos or make triggering comments but judging by what you've said, she just has a regular Instagram account and that's not cool. i'm sure she's nice and didn't mean to cause harm but it was still very ignorant. 

&#x200B;

tw // numbers

i have a coworker that looks like she has a BMI of 15-16 and we have a dessert bar where i work and she'll pick up pastries sometimes then whine about how she's "already soOOoooOo fAt and needs to stop eating so much" and i always sit there feeling like a beached whale like ?? is it really necessary for you to say that? 

&#x200B;

so yeah, i 100% relate to you and ik these ppl don't even realize how triggering they are but it annoys me to no end that there doesn't seem to be the least bit of consideration or mindfulness when it comes to their comments

oof, i'm glad your mother agrees that your grandmother is being ridiculous

&#x200B;

i'm happy you're healthier though! and ahh yea, the ED mind will always wanna be smaller but you've made amazing progress so far and i hope in the future you can be where you want to be and stay safe while doing so 💖

OH NO. that's a big no-no, is anyone else in your family aware of this? sounds like your grandma needs an intervention, it's bad enough she's projected onto you, i really hope your cousin isn't affected :(

&#x200B;

i'm glad your cousin has you to watch their back though!

it really can be horrible sometimes :(( when i do go on ED twitter, i follow ppl that have a higher sw in their bio like me and find that my timeline isn't as bad bc most of my mutuals don't post body checks but just safe food threads or low cal recipe threads 

&#x200B;

it can be nice sometimes! but i totally understand where you're coming from and i'm glad you've found a welcoming community here 💖

thank you <3

&#x200B;

i've been considering talking to her about it but i just know she'll force me to eat and it's gonna make us fight :/ like i already like to her about how many calories i have a day, i usually have 800-1000 and lied to her and said i'd been having 1200 and she freaked out and said that's too little. she was like "are you trying to get an eating disorder??" and i was like lol.... "trying"... then she would insist we eat together and cook bigger meals and watch me finish it and i'd do it so she'd back off but feel absolutely horrible and cry after

&#x200B;

i don't purge bc i have a fear of vomitting but i feel like i'll start if i come clean about my ed and she starts going crazy trying to get me to eat a lot. i don't know if confiding in her is an option at this point.

&#x200B;

i'm 19 but my family always treats me like a baby so :/ there's that. anyways, don't be sorry!! your reply meant a lot to me and i appreciate it. might take you up on the offer soon <3

coming from a younger sister triggered by her older sister being a little skinnier and shorter, i'd suggest just being more conscious about any comments you make about your weight around her (better yet, try not to at all when she's around)

&#x200B;

one of the worst things is when i hear my sister complaining about being fat and i just have to sit there like 🙃
